    {
      "id": "ohlcv-1h-master",
      "schema": "ohlcv-1h",
      "symbolSets": ["MASTER"],
      "start": "historyFloor",
      "end": "latest",
      "load": true,
      "splitSymbols": true,
      "splitDuration": "year",
      "append": true,
      "order": 2,
      "note": "Explicit MASTER symbols rather than ALL_SYMBOLS: ALL_SYMBOLS cannot be combined with split_symbols, and a symbol outside our master cannot be mapped to a listingId, so every one of them would quarantine. splitDuration is `year` rather than `none`, and the reason is NOT shard cost \u2014 the two are identical there, because the loader closes a buffer on a year change (`buf.year !== year`) as well as at the cap, so a whole-history file still writes one shard per symbol-year. `none` would be a quarter of the files (14,055 against 56,220). It is refused because it would cost the LOAD ORDER: stepLoad sorts newest-first off the session date in the vendor's filename, and a file spanning the entire history carries no date to sort on, so every file would tie and an interrupted backfill would survive holding an arbitrary slice instead of the recent end. With the download step running a bounded-concurrency pool the file count is no longer the binding constraint, so there is nothing left to buy with that trade."
    },
